No — the rename of mgm to gm has not been applied everywhere. Remaining occurrences include:

• Line 192:  
    MutableGraphModel mgm = (MutableGraphModel) gm;  
  → should be renamed to  
    MutableGraphModel gm = (MutableGraphModel) gmModel;  
  (and adjust the variable used in the rest of the method accordingly)

• Line 242:  
    MutableGraphModel mgm = (MutableGraphModel) gm;  
  → same renaming as above, and update references on lines 244–248, 279–280.

• Method addIncomingTrans signature (lines 306–309):  
    public Object addIncomingTrans(MutableGraphModel mgm, MStateVertex cls, MStateVertex newCls) {  
        return mgm.connect(newCls, cls, MTransition.class);  
    }  
  → rename parameter mgm to gm (or another non-conflicting name) and update the connect call.

• Calls within buttonClicked for addOutgoingTrans/addIncomingTrans still pass an mgm variable; those should be updated to the renamed variable.

After these edits, all local variables and parameters named mgm (and their usages) will be consistently renamed to gm (or another clear identifier) without touching external APIs.  
